  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">PayPal is proud to join the <a class="link" href="https://be.linkedin.com/company/european-payments-council?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>European Payments Council (EPC)</a>. 

As digital commerce continues to evolve, collaboration across the payments ecosystem has never been more important. European Payments Council membership reflects PayPal's commitment to advancing innovation, interoperability, trust, and resilience across the European payments landscape. 

In a new interview with the European Payments Council, Sean Byrne, CEO of PayPal Europe, shares perspectives on the future of payments in Europe, the growing importance of interoperability, and the opportunities that come from deeper industry collaboration. 

Read the full interview: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/ezr3iFWu?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/ezr3iFWu</a></p>
<!---->  </div>



        

        
            
      
    
    
    

